# Restly Clean Architecture

Follow Simple Skills kit in `.agents/` and skills under `.cursor/skills/` (especially `architecture-patterns`, `web-component-design`, `javascript-testing-patterns`).

## Layer map (frontend-first)

Dependencies point **inward only**. Outer layers may import inner; never the reverse.

```
src/
  app/                  # bootContainer(), router, React providers, Zustand
  application/
    ports/              # driven ports (API interfaces)
    use-cases/          # biz logic — framework-free
    query-keys.ts       # TanStack key factories
  pages/                # thin route screens
  features/<feature>/
    ui/                 # presentational React
    model/              # resolve(DI) + TanStack hooks
    lib/                # feature-local pure helpers
  entities/             # domain types + Zod — no React
  shared/               # constants, lib, styles — no feature imports
  infrastructure/
    adapters/           # port implementations
    di/                 # module-level container (NOT React Context)
    mock/ query/
```

## Rules

1. **Domain (`entities/`)** — plain TypeScript + Zod. No React, no DOM, no Zustand, no DI runtime.
2. **Application** — ports + use-cases only. No React, no concrete adapters.
3. **Features** — `ui` presentational; `model` resolves use-cases and wires TanStack. No feature→feature deep imports.
4. **Pages** — compose features; no business rules; no `fetch`.
5. **Infrastructure** — adapters implement ports; register in `createAppContainer`. UI never imports adapters.
6. **DI** — `bootContainer()` in `main.tsx`. Resolve via `resolve(TOKENS.*)`. Never React Context for the container. See `di.mdc`.
7. Zustand stores are **UI adapters**, not the domain.
8. Comments in source: English. Chat: `.agents/settings.yaml` `language`.
9. Lint/format with **OXC**: `npm run lint`, `npm run fmt`.

## When scaffolding or refactoring

1. Read `.agents/START_HERE.md` and `.agents/SKILL_PREAMBLE.md`.
2. Use skill `architecture-patterns` for Clean / Hexagonal guidance.
3. Follow `.cursor/rules/code-organization.mdc`, `constants.mdc`, `react-features.mdc`, `di.mdc`, `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md`.
